WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.580
The tech hiring process is broken.

2
00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:06.180
For employers, it's slow, expensive, and risky.

3
00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:08.420
Most companies end up having a bad hire

4
00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:12.180
that does not perform well as they did in the hiring interview.

5
00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:16.420
Developers get rejected randomly without any explanation or feedback.

6
00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:19.500
Also, it's harder than ever to prove your skills are real,

7
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:24.700
especially in the age of AI-generated code and glossy portfolios.

8
00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:28.460
Image if you can do one interview and don't have to do any other interviews

9
00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:32.740
because you already interviewed for the positions you are applying.

10
00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:34.780
That's why we're building Skill Verdict,

11
00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:39.180
a decentralized platform where developers verify for other skills.

12
00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:41.020
Here's how it works.

13
00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:45.530
A developer creates their profile and requests verification for specific skills

14
00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:46.980
or a project.

15
00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:50.820
They're matched with a qualified peer, for example, a senior engineer from

16
00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:51.420
Google

17
00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:55.310
who puts those skills to the test through a real-world project and live

18
00:00:55.310 --> 00:00:57.060
technical discussion,

19
00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:00.700
fully customized to the developer who is being tested.

20
00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:04.380
When they pass, the skill earns a permanent verified badge

21
00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:08.300
and can be proudly displayed in their CV 2.0.

22
00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.860
For companies, this means no more guesswork,

23
00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:15.560
just verified, reliable talent, which saves costs and time,

24
00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:18.420
even possibly skipping steps in the hiring process

25
00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:22.680
or the whole hiring process overall since the candidate has already been

26
00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:23.620
interviewed.

27
00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:28.300
For developers, it's a fair shot to stand out, no matter where you're from.

28
00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:31.100
Everyone deserves an equal chance.

29
00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:36.700
Our process is unbiased and anonymous and designed to be 100% fair.

30
00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:40.620
We're creating a meritocratic system where what you can do is proven

31
00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:44.700
and anyone, anywhere, can be recognized for it.

32
00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:49.900
Our current CV system is outdated and desperately needs an upgrade to CV 2.0,

33
00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:51.500
which we are building.

34
00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:54.980
The future of hiring is built on trust, not on AI.

35
00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:56.700
Don't chase a tract.

